# Twinflame Travelers' "Elemental" is a word of its text (CR 612): Artificial Evolution replacing Elemental with Merfolk in
# it makes it a Merfolk Sorcerer whose rule reads "another Merfolk you control". Casting the Evolution on turn 3, still
# under the old text, makes Hydro-Man, Fluid Felon's "Whenever you cast a blue spell, if Hydro-Man is a creature, he gets
# +1/+1" trigger twice; Emry, Lurker of the Loch, a blue spell cast after the change, once (Hydro-Man 5/5). Emry, a
# Merfolk, then enters and its "mill four cards" triggers twice: eight cards milled.
# Turn 1: Black Lotus (UUU) pays Hydro-Man's {U}{U}; the floating {U}, Mox Ruby, Mox Sapphire and the Volcanic Island pay
# the Travelers. Turn 3: Mox Sapphire pays the Evolution; Emry costs {U} with two artifacts (the Moxen), paid by the
# Volcanic Island. Bot1's graveyard: the Lotus, the Evolution and eight milled.

